# Implementation Plan - Module 6: Reporting & Audit Module

Implement a fully interactive, production-ready Reporting & Audit Dashboard matching the Stitch design (Screen ID `7514e431603942a5a46ce2d77719ee58`). This dashboard features dynamic filtering, live database-driven analytics aggregation, an immutable audit trail feed, and on-demand report compiling.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Interactive Filters Panel**: Add a top filter panel in `ReportingTab.tsx` with selectors for Department, Expense Category, Employee, and Date Range. Clicking "Apply Filters" will reload stats dynamically.
> - **Backend Stats Aggregator**: Introduce a new `GET /api/v1/reports/stats` API endpoint that computes department-wise spend, compliance percentages, variance calculations, and category breakdowns.
> - **Dynamic Audit Logs**: Upgrade the backend `getAuditLogs()` to query the expenses database, generating a timeline of submissions, approvals, and rejections.

## Proposed Changes

### Backend Components

---

#### [MODIFY] [reporting.module.ts](file:///d:/vibe%20code/spend-managment/project/backend/src/modules/reporting/reporting.module.ts)
- Import `UsersModule` to allow resolving department memberships and user names.

#### [MODIFY] [reporting.service.ts](file:///d:/vibe%20code/spend-managment/project/backend/src/modules/reporting/reporting.service.ts)
- Inject `UsersService` in constructor.
- Implement `getStats(filters: any)`:
  - Fetch all expenses and users.
  - Filter expenses by `filters.department`, `filters.categoryId`, `filters.employeeId`, and date thresholds (Time Period).
  - Aggregate spend by department: `{ Engineering, Marketing, Sales, Operations, HR, R&D }`.
  - Aggregate spend by category: `{ 'Travel & Subsistence', 'Software SaaS', 'Office Equipment' }`.
